1
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:06,759
(Howard:)It's amazing people keep coming
to comic book stores...

2
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:10,303
...instead ofjust downloading
comics digitally.

3
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:11,798
(Leonard:)It's probably for the best.

4
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:14,260
(Leonard:)For a lot of these guys,
the weekly trip here...

5
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:17,771
(Leonard:)...is the only chance their mom has to go
to the basement and change their sheets.

6
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,523
(Howard:)Oh, that reminds me,
I get fresh sheets tonight. Yay.

7
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:28,315
Well, what do you think
of new comic book night?

8
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,820
(Sheldon:)Magic, huh?

9
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,697
(Amy:)Sheldon, I'm disappointed.

10
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:35,036
(Amy:)As a brilliant man,
you're entitled to a vice.

11
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:37,371
(Amy:)I could understand frequenting
an opium den...

12
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:40,167
(Amy:)...or hunting your fellow man
for sport.

13
00:00:40,331 --> 00:00:43,421
(Amy:)But this? Lame-o.

14
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:48,171
(Sheldon:)A, comic books employ storytelling
through sequential art...

15
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:52,089
(Sheldon:)...a medium that dates back 17,000 years
to the cave paintings of Lascaux...

16
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,760
(Sheldon:)...and B, you play the harp,
Iike that's cool.

17
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:01,519
(Stuart:)Can I help you find anything?

